itary targets so why is Russia keep  doing it I think there's three main  reasons one of which is to try and erode  the will of the population it may be  cold in the UK it's fearsomely cold out  in uh in Ukraine at the moment and  therefore if you make life as miserable  as possible for the population  potentially undermines support for  zielinski in reality it seems to have  quite the opposite effect second reason  is that Russia's  retribution because things are not going  well for the Russians on the battlefield  they've given up 50 of the territory  that they once had taken and also the  ukrainians have effectively targeted the  Engels Air Force Base you know  comfortably some way behind the front  line and thirdly it's momentum Russia  needs momentum on the battlefield it  needs to buy time it needs to buy time  to rearm retrain re-equip and get ready  for a spring offensive and if you can  distract the Ukrainian military by  having to track and then shoot down all  these missiles potentially that's  another reason why they're doing it and  can I just go back to something we  mentioned at the start of this and that  was the attack on the temporary Russian  Barracks inside Ukraine what more are we  hearing about that attack  well yes it was a Ukrainian strike on a  a Russian military concentration point  it was happened at makiefke here which  you'll see is literally only about 13  kilometers away from the front line so  it's very very close the attack was done  using the Ukrainian high mass system  which has been provided by the American  it's been used since about June of the  year it's got about 100 kilometers at  range the ukrainians as you say claim  that they have killed 400 Russians and  300 casualties in response the Russians  have said that they uh they acknowledge  the attack they say two of the six  missiles that were fired they managed to  shoot down but four got through and they  admit that 63 Russians lost their lives  now in this information War what  actually happened is actually very  difficult for us to say what is  interesting is that Russians rarely turn  around and confirm any reports like this  so the very fact they've admitted it is  very telling and also independent  sources we're seeing some of the  wreckage here independent sources say  that about over 600 military personnel  were to be present in this facility so  it's quite feasible that there were  large number of casualties I think the  two main points come from this for me  one of which is the use of precisional  weapons by Ukraine provided by the West  Russian at the moment is provide is  using 20 000 artillery rounds a day  carpet bombing they're unguided with  limited effects apart from just  devastating everywhere around them  whereas the use of position weapons are  Salva four weapons can actually have a  devastating effect on the battlefield  and the second point I would make is  that this is a really good example of  what happens when you use conscript Army  that ill-experienced ill-equipped  ill-trained and lacking the right  equipment because first of all they  should not have all been collecting at a  point so close to the front line and  secondly if reports are to be believed  many of the conscripts will use their  own mobile phones they are very easily  tracked and once you get a collection of  those together that will be all the  intelligence that will be needed to make  that a key Focus for an attack so it's a  really clear lesson which the Russians  have paid a huge price for not learning  yeah clearly as you can see from these  scenes I'm Sean thank you Sean Bell
 

